## PR Title
[ACTION] Support Sendgrid Actions

## PR Description
This is a new PR for Sendgrid Actions. The previous [one](https://github.com/PipedreamHQ/pipedream/issues/1248) had modified unintendedly Reddit and Mailgun files.

Is there a specific app this action is for?
Sendgrid

Add Emails to Global Suppression | Adds recipient email address to the global suppression group.
Add or Update a Contact | Creates new contact or updates existing based on the email address.
Add or Update a Recipient (Legacy) | Adds a new recipient or updates an existing one based on the email address.
Add Recipients to a List (Legacy) | Adds existing recipients to a list.
Create a List | Creates a new list.
Delete a Global Suppression | Removes an email address from the global suppressions group.
Delete a List | Deletes a list.
Delete all Bounces | Deletes all bounces.
Delete Blocks | Deletes either all or specific emails on your block list.
Delete Bounces | Deletes specified bounces.
Delete Contacts | Deletes one or more contacts.
Delete Recipient from a List (Legacy) | Deletes recipient from a specific list.
Delete Recipients (Legacy) | Deletes one or more recipients.
Get a Block | Retrieves a specific email address from your block list.
Get a Global Suppression | Retrieves a specific global suppression email.
Make an API Call | Performs an arbitrary authorized API call.
Remove Contacts from a List | Removes contacts from the given list. The contacts will not be deleted.
Send an Email | Sends an email.
Validate an Email | Validates an email address.
Get all Bounces | Retrieves all of your bounces.
Get all Contacts | Retrieves all your contacts.
Get all Lists | Retrieves all your contact lists.
Get all Recipients | Retrieves all of your recipients or recipients under a specified list.
List Blocks | Lists all email addresses that are currently on your block list.
List Global Suppressions | Lists all email addresses that are globally suppressed.
Search Contacts | Searches for contacts.

Please provide a link to the relevant API docs for the specific service / operation.
https://sendgrid.com/docs/api-reference/
For Legacy endpoints: https://www.twilio.com/docs/sendgrid/api/v2/using_the_web_api

