## PR Title
NET-763: DHT control layer

## PR Description
<!--- Provide a general summary of the changes -->
This PR contains a new package called `dht`. The DHT will replace the trackers as peer discoverability layer and control layer transport.

The DHT is based on kademlia and uses the `k-bucket` library as its data structure.

The RPC protocol is based on protobuf and gRPC. All RPC messages are auto generated utilizing the `ts-protobuf` library. gRPC is not directly used as it is very transport dependant. Instead the gRPC generated interfaces are used to create a new transport independent RPC stack. The RPC stack can use any module that implements the `ITransport` interface as it Transport layer. Currently the ConnectionManager and DhtNode implement this inteface.

The DHT is structured in layers so that multiple DHTs can be stack on top of each other effortlessly. This enables the Layer 0 - Layer 1 design intended for the trackerless network.

The package is already browser compatible and is able to form WebRTC or WebSocket connections based on PeerDescriptions.

