## PR Title
Ksql cluster clean up

## PR Description
### Description 
This PR adds a new REST endpoint (`ksql/terminate`) to the KSQL server that is used to terminate a KSQL interactive cluster along with cleaning up the resources.
When a `TERMINATE CLUSTER` request is received by this end point, It will write it into the command topic. 
When each server reads this message from the command topic, no new request will be accepted after this statement.
The server will initialize the clean up process as the following:
1. All of the running queries will be terminated and cleaned up.
2. All of the Streams/Tables in the metastore along with their corresponding kafka topics will be deleted. 
3. The command topic will be deleted.

Note that if you don't want to delete all the streams/tables in the metastore you can add a list of strings with the key = `KEEP_SOURCES`  to the request parameters indicates the streams/tables with the names in the list should not be deleted.
Similarly, you can add a list of string with the key = `DELETE_SOURCES` indicating only the streams/tables in the list should be deleted and the rest of the stream/tables in the metastore won't be deleted.

-------------------------------
This PR is updated with the following changes in the design:

For clean up we should shut down all servers except one and send the cluster termination request using the corresponding REST end point, `/terminate`. The terminate request can include a list parameter, `DELETE_TOPIC_LIST`, that can contain a list of regex patterns. The kafka topics that match these patterns will be deleted during the termination process.

The following steps will be taken:
1. All of the running queries will be terminated and cleaned up.
2. If the terminate request include the `DELETE_TOPIC_LIST`, the kafka topics that match these patterns will be deleted. 
3. The command topic will be deleted.

Some refactoring also was done. A new class, `CommandTopicUtil`, was added to handle operations related to the command topic including the corresponding consumer/producer. The `CommandTopicUtil` instance now belongs to `CommandStore` class for improved encapsulation.

### Testing done 
Unit test was added.

